onl-vendor-config-onl (2.0.1) RELEASED; urgency=low

  * Python 2/3 Compatibility Fixes (2025-11-20) - COMPREHENSIVE
    - Fixed exception syntax: except Exception, e → except Exception as e
    - Fixed file() calls: file() → open()
    - Fixed print statements: print "text" → print("text")
    - Fixed dict iterators: .iteritems() → .items(), .iterkeys() → .keys(), .itervalues() → .values()
    - Fixed relative imports: import Fit → from . import Fit
    - Fixed StringIO compatibility: Added shim for Python 2/3
    - Fixed yaml.load(): Added Loader=yaml.SafeLoader argument
    - Fixed types.DictType: types.DictType → isinstance(x, dict)
    - Fixed string.rjust(): string.rjust(s, n) → s.rjust(n)
    - Fixed raw_input(): Added try/except for Python 2/3 compatibility
    - Added missing sys import to boot script
    - All Python files now compatible with both Python 2.7 and Python 3.11
    - Added compatibility headers to all modified files
    - Comprehensive scan performed to catch all Python 2-only constructs

  * Platform Detection Fixes
    - Added platform.baseconfig() call to boot script 51.onl-platform-baseconf
    - Ensures platform-specific ONLP implementation is loaded correctly

  * Boot System Fixes
    - Fixed merged-usr compatibility (moved overlay files from /sbin to /usr/sbin)
    - Fixed swiprep to use mount+tar instead of unsquashfs (preserves symlinks)

  * Files Modified: 23 total
    - 14 Python library files in onl/ modules
    - 4 bin scripts
    - 1 boot script
    - 4 additional files for new compatibility issues

